On Thu, 24 Jan 2007, azgor wrote:

> [1]: Rock traps aren't strong enough in later levels. Implement falling
> boulder traps.

A metal helmet protects you from falling boulders (see scrolls of earth).

> [4]: A cursed magic whistle should teleport random monsters on the level
> to you.

Hmm. Nice idea. I suppose it would not work on no-teleport levels
(Otherwise you could just teleport the wizard out of his tower, for
example.). And all teleported monsters should become angry (Otherwise you
just summon a shopkeeper and proceed to loot his shop, or you summon a
priest to convert the altar.).

> [5]: The other three corners of the castle should have mimics
> pretending to be chests. --aioli

A fitting but irrelevant idea: At this point, most characters already have
telepathy. Besides, if you manage to make your way into one corner, you
will have no problems checking out the other corners.

> [11]: If you're a canine, you should not see in color. --BenUrban

The colours are just part of the interface. A gnome lord does not differ
from a gnome in that he is shining in blue whereas normal gnomes are
brown, but in that he is wearing regal attire, which is symbolised on the
tty display with a particular colour.

